micq 0.4.3: stop the retronet ICQ window scrolling for ever.

micq talks to the museum gateway (Retro AIM Server, legacy ICQ v5 door on UDP 4000)
and keeps a contact-list refresh on a timer. The gateway answers each refresh with a
full presence dump and another SRV_X1 "list done" ack, and it never acknowledges
three of the client commands micq queues (Finish Login, Contact List, Delete Server
Messages). Stock micq treats all of that as news, so an idle station prints, roughly
every ten seconds and for ever:

  <nick> (Online) logged on.          for every contact
  ============ 18400: Your status is Online ... Users online: ...
  Discarded a Contact List packet.

None of it means anything is wrong -- the station signs in, sees its roster and
exchanges messages. But on an exhibit the ICQ window never stops scrolling, so the
framebuffer never settles: the golden bake has no stable frame to capture and an
idle station streams changed tiles all day.

Three surgical changes, each keeping the case that IS news:

  icq_response.c  announce a presence TRANSITION only; a repeat of a status we
                  already hold is silent.
  server.c        print the login summary once, when SRV_X1 actually means
                  "you are signed in", not on every later refresh ack.
  sendmsg.c       a routine unacked command is silent (including its newline and
                  redraw); a discarded LOGIN or KEEP_ALIVE -- which really does mean
                  the session is gone -- stays loud and still exits.

Applied by scripts/build-guests/tiles/slackware/compose.sh to /usr/src/micq, where the
guest's own gcc 2.7.2.3 builds it (docs/lab/retronet/STATION-slackware.md).

--- a/icq_response.c
+++ b/icq_response.c
@@ -299,6 +299,21 @@
    
    if ( Done_Login )
    {
+      /* Kernel Hive (retronet): micq refreshes its contact list every few seconds,
+         and the museum gateway answers EVERY refresh with a full presence dump
+         rather than only transitions. Stock micq therefore reprints
+         "<nick> (Online) logged on." for every contact roughly every ten seconds,
+         and the station's ICQ window scrolls for ever — an exhibit that never
+         settles and a framebuffer that never stops changing. Announce a real
+         TRANSITION only; a repeat of a status we already hold is silent. */
+      {
+         CONTACT_PTR kh_c = UIN2Contact( remote_uin );
+         if ( kh_c != NULL && kh_c->status == new_status )
+         {
+            kh_c->last_time = time( NULL );
+            return;
+         }
+      }
 /*      M_print( "\n" );*/
       R_undraw();
       M_print( CONTACTCOL );
--- a/server.c
+++ b/server.c
@@ -150,7 +150,13 @@
       if ( Verbose ) {
          M_print( "Acknowleged SRV_X1 0x021C Done Contact list?\n" );
       }
-      Show_Quick_Online_Status();
+      /* Kernel Hive (retronet): SRV_X1 is the server's "contact list done" ack, and
+         the museum gateway sends it again on every periodic contact-list refresh,
+         not just at login. Stock micq redraws the whole online-users block each
+         time, so the station's ICQ window repaints for ever. Print the summary
+         once, when it actually means "you are signed in". */
+      if ( !Done_Login )
+         Show_Quick_Online_Status();
      /* Show_Quick_Status();*/
       R_redraw ();
       Done_Login = TRUE;
--- a/sendmsg.c
+++ b/sendmsg.c
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
     char *temp;
     char url_desc[1024], url_data[1024];
     net_icq_pak pak;
+    int kh_silent = 0;   /* Kernel Hive: see the discard branch below */
 
     if ((queued_msg = msg_queue_pop()) != NULL)
     {
@@ -113,17 +114,34 @@
                    M_print( NOCOL " " );
                }
             } else {
-	       M_print( "\nDiscarded a " );
-	       Print_CMD( Chars_2_Word( pak.head.cmd ) );
-	       M_print( " packet." );
-	       if ( ( CMD_LOGIN == Chars_2_Word( pak.head.cmd ) ) ||
-	            ( CMD_KEEP_ALIVE == Chars_2_Word( pak.head.cmd ) ) ) {
+	       /* Kernel Hive (retronet): the museum gateway acknowledges sign-in and
+	          presence but NOT every client command micq queues -- Finish Login,
+	          Contact List and Delete Server Messages go unacked. micq retries each
+	          six times and then reports the discard, and because it refreshes its
+	          contact list on a timer that report repeats for ever, in the exhibit's
+	          ICQ window. Nothing is actually broken: the station signs in, sees its
+	          roster and exchanges messages. So keep the one case that IS fatal
+	          (a discarded login or keep-alive means the session is gone) loud, and
+	          let the routine ones be silent -- including the trailing newline and
+	          redraw, which would otherwise scroll the window on their own. */
+	       int kh_fatal = ( ( CMD_LOGIN == Chars_2_Word( pak.head.cmd ) ) ||
+	                        ( CMD_KEEP_ALIVE == Chars_2_Word( pak.head.cmd ) ) );
+	       if ( kh_fatal || Verbose ) {
+	          M_print( "\nDiscarded a " );
+	          Print_CMD( Chars_2_Word( pak.head.cmd ) );
+	          M_print( " packet." );
+	       } else {
+	          kh_silent = 1;
+	       }
+	       if ( kh_fatal ) {
                   M_print( "\n\aConnection unstable. Exiting...." );
 		  Quit = TRUE;
 	       }
 	    }
-	    M_print ("\n");
-	    R_redraw ();
+	    if ( !kh_silent )
+	       M_print ("\n");
+	    R_redraw ();   /* always: it is the symmetric half of the R_undraw above,
+	                      and it repaints the Micq> prompt in place without scrolling */
 
             free(queued_msg->body);
             free(queued_msg);
